From: SAGIT Port <sagit@local>
Subject: [PATCH] zalloc: use embedded zone map sizes for SAGIT

The build uses XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX, so zalloc reserves the macOS zone map
(128GB VA, 32GB max).  That works on the large-memory 16K layout, whose
kernel map spans more than a terabyte, but the 4K non-large layout only
provides about 48GiB between VM_MIN_KERNEL_ADDRESS and
VM_MAX_KERNEL_ADDRESS, so kmem_range_init could not place the zones claim:

  kmem_range_init: vm_map_locate_space failing for claim zones

Use the embedded (iOS) 24GB/8GB numbers, which do fit alongside the
compressor and the other claims.
---
 osfmk/kern/zalloc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c b/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c
@@ -163,4 +163,4 @@
-#if XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX
+#if XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SAGIT)
 #define ZONE_MAP_MAX            (32ULL << 30)
 #define ZONE_MAP_VA_SIZE        (128ULL << 30)
 #else /* XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX */
